# Line endings, settled once.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true writes CRLF into the
# working copy while the repo stores LF, so every line of every text file reads
# as modified with byte-identical content -- two dozen phantom diffs hiding the
# one real edit, and `git add -A` unusable. `text=auto` still lets git detect
# binaries and leave them alone; `eol=lf` pins the working copy to what the repo
# already holds, on every platform. Same settings as the Assignment Maker repo.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the image and font assets under logos/ and public/, so no
# future detection change can rewrite one of them a line at a time.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
